1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:01,876
<i>Hello?</i>

2
00:00:01,960 --> 00:00:03,420
<i>Do something.</i>

3
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:04,963
<i>If not, you'll get dragged into this.</i>

4
00:00:05,046 --> 00:00:07,632
<i>We all know that fake news is everywhere.</i>

5
00:00:08,216 --> 00:00:10,343
<i>This isn't just an ordinary issue.</i>

6
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:11,511
<i>This is a crime.</i>

7
00:00:11,594 --> 00:00:14,597
<i>So whoever you are</i>
<i>who's trying to mess with us,</i>

8
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:15,807
<i>no matter where you are,</i>

9
00:00:15,890 --> 00:00:17,392
<i>I'll find you.</i>

10
00:00:17,475 --> 00:00:19,185
<i>Hi, this is Billy speaking.</i>

11
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:21,396
<i>Oh my gosh, Ms. Billy!</i>
<i>Is that really you?</i>

12
00:00:21,479 --> 00:00:23,273
[BILLY] <i>Abi, it's you.</i>

13
00:00:23,356 --> 00:00:24,941
[ABI] <i>Congratulations again!</i>

14
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,776
<i>You're amazing, idol!</i>

15
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,486
<i>It's so soft!</i>

16
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:30,864
<i>Must be nice.</i>

17
00:00:31,740 --> 00:00:33,116
[BIRDS CHIRPING]

18
00:00:34,492 --> 00:00:36,119
Wow. I didn't know you had a fan.

19
00:00:36,202 --> 00:00:37,704
[SCOFFS] Don't be silly.

20
00:00:37,787 --> 00:00:40,081
I just feel sorry for Abi.

21
00:00:40,165 --> 00:00:44,043
Auntie Pres, listen to this.

22
00:00:44,127 --> 00:00:47,589
She said her father
and sister abandoned her.

23
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:50,425
She was left all alone
to take care of her mother.

24
00:00:51,009 --> 00:00:52,802
I told her

25
00:00:52,886 --> 00:00:56,431
that maybe she needs to take a break.

26
00:00:56,514 --> 00:00:57,849
Go on vacation.

27
00:00:57,932 --> 00:01:00,977
She could get a caregiver for her mom.

28
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:03,396
Correct. Why doesn't she do that?

29
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:04,731
I don't think she can afford to.

30
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:08,068
I think their business
is struggling or something.

31
00:01:08,151 --> 00:01:11,112
[BILLY] I want to help her, Auntie Pres.

32
00:01:11,196 --> 00:01:14,365
I feel a sense of…

33
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,034
It's not pity.

34
00:01:16,951 --> 00:01:18,870
Maybe potential?

35
00:01:19,996 --> 00:01:21,331
Connection?

36
00:01:24,250 --> 00:01:25,293
[GASPS]

37
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:28,880
Wait a minute.

38
00:01:29,964 --> 00:01:31,007
[GUSHES]

39
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:37,889
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

40
00:01:52,070 --> 00:01:53,988
Listen to me, Benilda.

41
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:57,408
You don't have to help
every woman in need.

42
00:01:58,159 --> 00:02:01,121
Don't you have
enough problems of your own to fix?

43
00:02:01,204 --> 00:02:03,540
Yes, I agree. Okay.

44
00:02:05,458 --> 00:02:07,085
Can we eat already?

45
00:02:07,168 --> 00:02:08,461
I'm hungry.

46
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:11,339
Did you hear that? That's a big problem.

47
00:02:11,422 --> 00:02:13,133
[BILLY] You got that right, Auntie Pres.

48
00:02:13,216 --> 00:02:15,343
- He calls the shots. Let's go.
- [JORDAN] Come on.

49
00:02:15,426 --> 00:02:17,470
Come on, let's go.

50
00:02:17,554 --> 00:02:24,060
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

51
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:26,771
Just need a pair of shoes.

52
00:02:26,855 --> 00:02:33,778
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:41,578 --> 00:02:42,745
[SPRITZING]

54
00:02:42,829 --> 00:02:49,085
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

55
00:02:58,887 --> 00:03:05,560
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

56
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:55,401
[INTRIGUING MUSIC PLAYING]

57
00:04:10,625 --> 00:04:17,632
[INTRIGUING MUSIC CONTINUES]

58
00:04:28,226 --> 00:04:30,853
[BILLY] Have you seen
my red shoes, Auntie?

59
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,231
The pair I wore
to the LoveList anniversary party.

60
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:34,482
No.

61
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:37,443
Goodness, Billy.

62
00:04:37,527 --> 00:04:39,153
You're becoming so forgetful.

63
00:04:39,237 --> 00:04:40,947
First, you lost your keys.

64
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:42,740
Now, it's your shoes.

65
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:44,284
Maybe you left them in the car.

66
00:04:44,367 --> 00:04:47,328
You leave spares in your car, right?

67
00:04:47,412 --> 00:04:50,456
You switch to rubber shoes
when your feet get sore.

68
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:51,499
No, Auntie.

69
00:04:51,582 --> 00:04:53,543
I remember that night,

70
00:04:53,626 --> 00:04:56,504
I got out of the car holding my shoes.

71
00:04:56,587 --> 00:04:58,089
Then where are they?

72
00:04:59,882 --> 00:05:02,468
[WOMAN 1] Wow! How beautiful!

73
00:05:03,761 --> 00:05:10,143
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:05:18,568 --> 00:05:20,778
[WOMAN 2] Looking good, miss!

75
00:05:20,862 --> 00:05:22,989
[MAN] Wow!

76
00:05:23,072 --> 00:05:24,240
[WOMAN 2] Did you see her?

77
00:05:28,536 --> 00:05:31,247
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:32,290
[GASPS]

79
00:05:36,711 --> 00:05:42,925
[DARK MUSIC CONTINUES]

80
00:05:48,014 --> 00:05:51,434
[MALE OFFICER]
Carlos Toledo, you're free to go.

81
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,102
Your bail has been posted.

82
00:05:54,687 --> 00:05:55,688
Huh?

83
00:05:55,772 --> 00:05:57,273
[LOCK CLANKING]

84
00:05:59,192 --> 00:06:00,443
[GRUNTS]

85
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:02,028
[DOOR HANDLE CRANKS]

86
00:06:02,111 --> 00:06:05,490
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

87
00:06:13,372 --> 00:06:14,916
It's all good now, ma'am. I've changed it.

88
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:17,251
Perfect! Thank you, mister.

89
00:06:17,335 --> 00:06:19,003
Here.

90
00:06:19,087 --> 00:06:20,296
Oh, wait.

91
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:23,049
- Thank you. Thank you.
- Thanks too.

92
00:06:26,385 --> 00:06:27,970
Paranoid much?

93
00:06:28,638 --> 00:06:30,098
Better safe than sorry, Auntie.

94
00:06:30,807 --> 00:06:32,558
I can't find my old key.

95
00:06:32,642 --> 00:06:34,602
- Someone might break in.
- [PHONE CHIMES]

96
00:06:34,685 --> 00:06:35,978
At least we're safe.

97
00:06:37,396 --> 00:06:38,606
[CHUCKLES]

98
00:06:39,690 --> 00:06:41,943
- Something interesting?
- Huh?

99
00:06:42,026 --> 00:06:44,612
It's your app.
It's really something.

100
00:06:44,695 --> 00:06:47,532
I keep receiving notifications. Uh, I…

101
00:06:47,615 --> 00:06:49,784
I accepted Brandon's request.

102
00:06:49,867 --> 00:06:52,245
Well, that's what happens when
you click "Accept."

103
00:06:52,328 --> 00:06:53,287
So how do you find Brandon?

104
00:06:53,371 --> 00:06:54,664
- Hmm?
- How do you find him?

105
00:06:54,747 --> 00:06:57,291
Well, he's a volunteer at the orphanage,

106
00:06:57,375 --> 00:07:01,963
and he seems active
in feeding programs for children.

107
00:07:02,046 --> 00:07:04,924
Plus, he's handsome, so that's a bonus.

108
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:08,261
You're perfect for each other.
He also likes to cook.

109
00:07:08,344 --> 00:07:10,596
You forgot to log out.

110
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:14,183
- [GASPS] Oh, you!
- [BILLY CHUCKLES]

111
00:07:14,267 --> 00:07:16,477
- [BILLY] Busted!
- You're so nosy.

112
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,312
- Hurry up and finish eating.
- [PHONE RINGING]

113
00:07:18,396 --> 00:07:19,897
The bus will be here soon.

114
00:07:19,981 --> 00:07:20,940
Hello?

115
00:07:21,023 --> 00:07:24,527
Dude, Caloy just posted bail.

116
00:07:24,610 --> 00:07:25,653
What?

117
00:07:25,736 --> 00:07:26,821
Come on. I'm on my way.

118
00:07:26,904 --> 00:07:33,411
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

119
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:37,331
[CALOY HUFFS]

120
00:07:38,708 --> 00:07:39,834
- Hey, man.
- Oh.

121
00:07:40,835 --> 00:07:41,961
You two again?

122
00:07:42,837 --> 00:07:44,380
Are you giving me a ride home?

123
00:07:44,964 --> 00:07:46,674
Who bailed you out?

124
00:07:47,967 --> 00:07:49,594
Was it your boss?

125
00:07:49,677 --> 00:07:52,805
How many times do I have to tell you both?

126
00:07:52,889 --> 00:07:54,891
I don't even know who my boss is!

127
00:07:54,974 --> 00:07:57,143
Someone just left the money
outside my house.

128
00:07:57,768 --> 00:07:58,769
Are we done here?

129
00:07:59,687 --> 00:08:02,148
Caloy, just tell us the truth.

130
00:08:02,231 --> 00:08:04,150
You haven't learned your lesson, have you?

131
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:06,194
Are you threatening us?

132
00:08:08,321 --> 00:08:11,324
We won't stop
until we send you back to jail.

133
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:12,742
And when that happens,

134
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:15,870
I'll make sure that you rot in there.

135
00:08:15,953 --> 00:08:17,371
You bastard!

136
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:18,789
You're also annoying.

137
00:08:19,707 --> 00:08:20,750
I could stab you, you know?

138
00:08:20,833 --> 00:08:22,585
- Don't you dare!
- Jordan.

139
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:26,255
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

140
00:08:26,339 --> 00:08:29,050
You're lucky I just got released.

141
00:08:32,220 --> 00:08:33,971
Otherwise, I would've let you two have it.

142
00:08:34,055 --> 00:08:40,686
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

143
00:08:46,317 --> 00:08:50,238
Her face is flawless, and she's so pretty.

144
00:08:50,321 --> 00:08:52,073
She has soft hands too.

145
00:08:52,156 --> 00:08:56,452
She has all these nice clothes,
makeup, and shoes.

146
00:08:57,161 --> 00:08:58,663
Plus, she smells good.

147
00:08:58,746 --> 00:09:00,164
She smells really good!

148
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:02,625
You're getting envious again.

149
00:09:02,708 --> 00:09:05,086
You're so jealous of her.

150
00:09:05,169 --> 00:09:09,382
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

151
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:11,008
It's not like that, Ma.

152
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:13,928
You see, she also has a nice car.

153
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:17,056
She has nice stuff,

154
00:09:17,139 --> 00:09:19,267
and her business is doing good.

155
00:09:19,850 --> 00:09:21,227
And it seems…

156
00:09:22,144 --> 00:09:23,688
she has a happy family.

157
00:09:24,689 --> 00:09:26,148
That made me wonder.

158
00:09:28,651 --> 00:09:30,695
Did she have a hard time in life?

159
00:09:32,196 --> 00:09:33,739
But I don't think so.

160
00:09:36,993 --> 00:09:40,413
She's a lucky woman. She's so lucky.

161
00:09:40,496 --> 00:09:42,665
She's very lucky.

162
00:09:44,375 --> 00:09:46,919
<i>Call your sister. Let's eat.</i>

163
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:54,927
<i>Ma, why are there only three plates?</i>

164
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:59,015
<i>I told you to call your sister.</i>

165
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:02,727
<i>Did you know she got promoted?</i>

166
00:10:03,769 --> 00:10:07,148
<i>Your sister is really amazing.</i>

167
00:10:07,231 --> 00:10:09,734
<i>She's so smart.</i>

168
00:10:12,403 --> 00:10:13,946
<i>Oh come on, Ma.</i>

169
00:10:14,030 --> 00:10:16,073
<i>I was just asking why</i>
<i>there were only three plates,</i>

170
00:10:16,157 --> 00:10:18,993
<i>and you keep blabbing about Abi.</i>

171
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:20,369
<i>So why are there only three plates?</i>

172
00:10:20,453 --> 00:10:24,081
<i>Is Papa not coming home?</i>
<i>Isn't he joining us?</i>

173
00:10:24,165 --> 00:10:28,669
<i>You are so dumb, aren't you?</i>

174
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,962
<i>You're stupid!</i>

175
00:10:31,255 --> 00:10:32,965
<i>You really take after your father.</i>

176
00:10:33,049 --> 00:10:35,051
<i>You're both useless!</i>

177
00:10:35,885 --> 00:10:37,136
<i>So, what?</i>

178
00:10:38,429 --> 00:10:40,973
<i>Are you going to take his side, huh?</i>

179
00:10:41,057 --> 00:10:44,769
<i>Then get out of here and go with him!</i>

180
00:10:44,852 --> 00:10:48,522
<i>You deserve each other anyway!</i>

181
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,400
[SCREAMING]

182
00:10:51,484 --> 00:10:52,443
[PLATES SHATTER]

183
00:10:52,526 --> 00:10:56,072
- [MARIELA SCREAMING]
- [PLATES SHATTER]

184
00:10:57,239 --> 00:11:02,953
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

185
00:11:03,037 --> 00:11:04,622
<i>What happened?</i>

186
00:11:04,705 --> 00:11:10,461
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

187
00:11:12,463 --> 00:11:19,178
[DARK MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:11:20,471 --> 00:11:22,014
[WIND WHOOSHING]

189
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:24,058
[FIRE CRACKLING]

190
00:11:24,141 --> 00:11:25,434
[ABIGAIL PANTING]

191
00:11:25,518 --> 00:11:28,437
<i>Ma! Ma!</i>

192
00:11:28,521 --> 00:11:31,190
[SCREAMING, PANTING]

193
00:11:31,273 --> 00:11:32,233
<i>Ma!</i>

194
00:11:33,401 --> 00:11:35,277
[ABIGAIL COUGHS]

195
00:11:35,361 --> 00:11:39,740
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [ABIGAIL BREATHING HEAVILY]

196
00:11:39,824 --> 00:11:41,242
- [THUD]
- [ABIGAIL WHIMPERS]

197
00:11:41,325 --> 00:11:42,159
<i>Ma!</i>

198
00:11:43,702 --> 00:11:44,829
<i>Ma!</i>

199
00:11:46,872 --> 00:11:53,754
- [TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [FIRE CRACKLING]

200
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:56,841
- [WOOD THUDS]
- [ABIGAIL GASPS]

201
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:58,926
[ABIGAIL PANTING]

202
00:12:01,929 --> 00:12:03,013
<i>Ma! Ma!</i>

203
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:06,100
<i>Ma.</i>

204
00:12:07,768 --> 00:12:08,853
[ABIGAIL GRUNTS]

205
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:09,895
<i>- Oh my God!</i>
<i>- Help!</i>

206
00:12:09,979 --> 00:12:12,106
<i>Ma! Ma!</i>

207
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:14,358
<i>- Take her.</i>
<i>- Ma.</i>

208
00:12:14,442 --> 00:12:16,485
<i>- Help her.</i>
<i>- Help! Ma.</i>

209
00:12:16,569 --> 00:12:20,030
<i>Ma, wake up! Ma!</i>

210
00:12:20,739 --> 00:12:21,907
<i>Ma.</i>

211
00:12:22,450 --> 00:12:24,660
[LABORED BREATHING]

212
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:26,120
<i>- Abigail.</i>
- [OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

213
00:12:26,203 --> 00:12:28,789
<i>Abigail! Abigail!</i>

214
00:12:28,873 --> 00:12:30,583
- [ABIGAIL BREATHING HEAVILY]
<i>- Abigail.</i>

215
00:12:31,333 --> 00:12:32,543
<i>Abigail.</i>

216
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:34,628
<i>Abigail.</i>

217
00:12:35,504 --> 00:12:36,964
<i>Abigail!</i>

218
00:12:37,047 --> 00:12:40,509
[MUSIC FADING]

219
00:12:45,681 --> 00:12:47,516
But don't worry, Ma.

220
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,437
Luck is finally on our side.

221
00:12:51,520 --> 00:12:52,980
It's close.

222
00:12:53,063 --> 00:12:55,024
I can feel it.

223
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:56,317
It's coming.

224
00:12:56,400 --> 00:13:00,905
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

225
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:05,743
You're still seriously hoping
things will get better?!

226
00:13:05,826 --> 00:13:09,121
You really are stupid,
just like your father.

227
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:14,210
You're so naïve,
to think that luck will find us.

228
00:13:14,293 --> 00:13:16,212
There's no hope for us! This is it!

229
00:13:16,295 --> 00:13:17,505
Look at me! Just look at me!

230
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:23,052
Your nose has longer hair than my head.

231
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:28,307
[LAUGHS]

232
00:13:28,390 --> 00:13:29,225
Right?

233
00:13:31,060 --> 00:13:33,562
[LAUGHS] Let me see your armpit.

234
00:13:33,646 --> 00:13:34,522
Let me see.

235
00:13:34,605 --> 00:13:35,523
[LAUGHS]

236
00:13:35,606 --> 00:13:36,982
You have a lot of hair.

237
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:38,734
[LAUGHTER]

238
00:13:38,817 --> 00:13:40,778
They're really long. I swear.

239
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:47,826
- [STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [MARIELA LAUGHING]

240
00:13:53,249 --> 00:13:57,169
Toledo was granted bail on the
grounds of self-defense.

241
00:13:57,253 --> 00:13:58,837
What?

242
00:13:58,921 --> 00:14:01,840
Attorney, we both know that's not true.

243
00:14:02,675 --> 00:14:05,302
What can we do to send him back to jail?

244
00:14:06,303 --> 00:14:11,433
Well, we can file a motion to revoke bail

245
00:14:11,517 --> 00:14:13,310
or a motion for reconsideration.

246
00:14:13,394 --> 00:14:16,230
- But it won't be easy, okay?
- Mm-hmm.

247
00:14:16,313 --> 00:14:19,191
We need to present a compelling reason,

248
00:14:19,275 --> 00:14:20,943
such as new evidence

249
00:14:21,026 --> 00:14:24,154
or a violation of bail conditions.

250
00:14:24,989 --> 00:14:29,618
For now, just make sure
you don't do anything illegal

251
00:14:29,702 --> 00:14:31,704
that Toledo might use against you.

252
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:36,500
[TRAFFIC NOISE]

253
00:14:37,793 --> 00:14:41,088
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

254
00:14:41,171 --> 00:14:44,967
Boss, this place feels sketchy.

255
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:47,136
You bet. Our boss got stabbed here.

256
00:14:47,803 --> 00:14:50,598
This seems like a bad decision.
Let's go, boss.

257
00:14:51,682 --> 00:14:54,602
That jerk threatened Billy. Come on.

258
00:14:57,187 --> 00:14:59,189
That's him! There he is!

259
00:15:02,484 --> 00:15:03,986
What's your plan?

260
00:15:04,069 --> 00:15:06,697
- Let's beat him up.
- Hey, what are you saying?

261
00:15:06,780 --> 00:15:10,034
We agreed that we'd resolve this
through peaceful dialogue.

262
00:15:10,117 --> 00:15:11,368
Seriously, boss?

263
00:15:11,452 --> 00:15:15,831
I love you, but my love has limits.

264
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:19,418
- Come on, let's beat him up.
- No, no, no. Not yet.

265
00:15:21,879 --> 00:15:24,173
Let's see where he goes.

266
00:15:24,757 --> 00:15:26,842
I'm scared.

267
00:15:26,926 --> 00:15:29,011
If I had beaten him up,
he wouldn't have reached the door.

268
00:15:29,094 --> 00:15:31,931
- He'd all be black and blue.
- Shh.

269
00:15:32,014 --> 00:15:33,557
Peaceful dialogue? Yeah, right.

270
00:15:34,600 --> 00:15:37,978
You have to be extra careful, Billy.

271
00:15:38,062 --> 00:15:40,564
How did that Caloy
even get released from jail?

272
00:15:41,357 --> 00:15:44,026
- He's got a strong backer.
- Mm-hmm.

273
00:15:44,109 --> 00:15:46,195
Thank you for your concern.

274
00:15:46,987 --> 00:15:49,573
Here. It wards off evil spirits.

275
00:15:49,657 --> 00:15:52,826
- You need that.
- Oh my God, guys! Look!

276
00:15:52,910 --> 00:15:58,290
My feature on LoveLine
got a million views in just 12 hours.

277
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,501
Wow! Nice, twinny Val!

278
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:02,419
How many views did you get?

279
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:06,799
I love your feature, twinny Val!

280
00:16:06,882 --> 00:16:08,676
Hopefully, we can do a collab next time

281
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:11,929
and make content
on Switch Lives with Blaire.

282
00:16:12,012 --> 00:16:13,847
It will be easy for you.

283
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:15,099
Let's go!

284
00:16:15,182 --> 00:16:17,226
You're a content creator too?

285
00:16:18,268 --> 00:16:19,937
Here.

286
00:16:20,020 --> 00:16:21,730
- Hmm.
- [BLAIRE] See?

287
00:16:22,481 --> 00:16:23,607
Wow.

288
00:16:23,691 --> 00:16:25,734
Our numbers are up. Right, Toni?

289
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:27,069
Oh, yes.

290
00:16:27,152 --> 00:16:29,947
Our engagement is up by 48%.

291
00:16:30,030 --> 00:16:33,117
Our ad clicks also doubled.

292
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:36,787
Billy, I'm sorry that
I had doubts about this before.

293
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:39,164
I mean, it's so risky to take a gamble

294
00:16:39,248 --> 00:16:42,126
on LoveLine without any investors.

295
00:16:42,209 --> 00:16:43,961
It was risky. Yes.

296
00:16:44,044 --> 00:16:46,797
But growth doesn't come
from playing safe, right?

297
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:51,468
Thank you all for taking the leap with me.

298
00:16:51,552 --> 00:16:53,846
That's what makes this team different.

299
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:57,391
So congratulations, and good job, girls.

300
00:16:57,474 --> 00:16:58,642
[CLAPPING, CHEERING]

301
00:16:58,726 --> 00:17:01,645
This calls for a group hug! Yes.

302
00:17:01,729 --> 00:17:04,857
- I want to join.
- Me too.

303
00:17:04,940 --> 00:17:08,485
- Fine. I'll join too.
- Group hug!

304
00:17:08,569 --> 00:17:10,154
- This is nice.
- Yeah.

305
00:17:10,237 --> 00:17:11,447
Okay.

306
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:22,916
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

307
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:36,305
Robbie, Rain, wake up.
He's leaving. Come on.

308
00:17:36,388 --> 00:17:38,974
- That way.
- Come on.

309
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:50,110
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

310
00:17:53,447 --> 00:17:54,656
Don't make any noise.

311
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,119
How are you?

312
00:18:00,829 --> 00:18:01,997
Are you okay?

313
00:18:08,378 --> 00:18:10,380
You really had to go back there?

314
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:11,757
Huh?

315
00:18:12,591 --> 00:18:14,301
- [BILLY] Hmm?
- [JORDAN] Who told you?

316
00:18:14,384 --> 00:18:17,638
We've got lots of customers.
They come at this hour.

317
00:18:19,723 --> 00:18:20,557
Well?

318
00:18:20,641 --> 00:18:23,185
Dude, before you get mad,

319
00:18:23,268 --> 00:18:25,771
we saw him talking to someone
inside a cab.

320
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:28,107
We don't know who it was,

321
00:18:28,774 --> 00:18:30,567
but that person handed him an envelope.

322
00:18:30,651 --> 00:18:33,362
So it's not true that Caloy
doesn't know who it is.

323
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,325
Did you get the license plate?

324
00:18:38,408 --> 00:18:42,996
Yes, ma'am, but the operator won't tell us
where the passenger was dropped off.

325
00:18:43,080 --> 00:18:44,540
We have to secure a court order first.

326
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:48,836
[RAIN] You know, I'm scared of Caloy.

327
00:18:48,919 --> 00:18:50,546
He looks like someone who can kill.

328
00:18:50,629 --> 00:18:54,133
Exactly. So promise me
you won't go back there, dude.

329
00:18:54,216 --> 00:18:55,134
It's dangerous.

330
00:18:55,843 --> 00:18:56,760
Hey.

331
00:18:57,845 --> 00:19:00,097
Come on, dude. You have to promise me.

332
00:19:02,683 --> 00:19:04,560
- Boss, make a promise.
- [BILLY] But thank you.

333
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:07,229
Thank you.

334
00:19:08,772 --> 00:19:10,607
[RAIN] Uh, Ma'am Billy…

335
00:19:11,191 --> 00:19:13,735
Where was Valerie around 7:00 p.m.?

336
00:19:14,319 --> 00:19:16,113
Seven? I'm not sure.

337
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:18,448
But I know she was already
out of the office.

338
00:19:18,532 --> 00:19:19,366
[ROBBIE] Oh.

339
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:23,579
Do you think it was Valerie?

340
00:19:23,662 --> 00:19:25,122
[RAIN] Yes. It's--

341
00:19:25,205 --> 00:19:27,666
I have a strong feeling that it was her.

342
00:19:28,584 --> 00:19:30,544
[ROBBIE GROANS] I don't know.

343
00:19:35,966 --> 00:19:41,763
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

344
00:19:41,847 --> 00:19:46,643
Hi there, Ms. Billy Idol.
I'm at your house.

345
00:19:46,727 --> 00:19:52,399
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

346
00:19:57,237 --> 00:20:00,199
- [DOORKNOB RATTLING]
- [KEYS JINGLING]

347
00:20:01,992 --> 00:20:04,536
[CHUCKLES] Oops. Wrong key.

348
00:20:06,747 --> 00:20:08,332
- Why won't it open?
- [DOORKNOB RATTLING]

349
00:20:09,333 --> 00:20:11,084
I used this key before.

350
00:20:11,168 --> 00:20:13,754
[DOORKNOB RATTLING]

351
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:21,136
- [DOORKNOB RATTLING]
- [KEYS JINGLING]

352
00:20:23,555 --> 00:20:25,015
Aah!

353
00:20:26,183 --> 00:20:31,980
- [TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]
- [BREATHING HEAVILY]

354
00:20:39,321 --> 00:20:46,286
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

355
00:21:05,347 --> 00:21:08,350
Yes, Freddie. We are open to sponsorships.

356
00:21:08,433 --> 00:21:12,562
We can play your ads
while on call waiting.

357
00:21:14,189 --> 00:21:16,400
Yes, we can also put your names

358
00:21:16,483 --> 00:21:18,902
as sponsors on the posters and billboards.

359
00:21:19,486 --> 00:21:20,570
Mall shows?

360
00:21:21,863 --> 00:21:22,906
Two years?

361
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:25,742
Yes, we can do that as well.

362
00:21:27,577 --> 00:21:28,620
Okay.

363
00:21:28,704 --> 00:21:29,955
I'll let you know. Thank you.

364
00:21:31,832 --> 00:21:34,084
[BRIGHT HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

365
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:36,420
Chief, are we on?

366
00:21:37,587 --> 00:21:39,339
Please tell me we have a deal.

367
00:21:44,261 --> 00:21:47,055
Yes. They'll send us the contract!

368
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:48,056
We have a deal!

369
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,225
- We have a deal!
- We have a deal!

370
00:21:50,309 --> 00:21:52,769
[JORDAN] We have a deal, baby! Let's go!

371
00:21:52,853 --> 00:21:54,521
- [APPLAUDING]
- Congratulations!

372
00:21:54,604 --> 00:21:56,523
- Thank you!
- Finally, some good news.

373
00:21:56,606 --> 00:21:59,818
[BILLY] See?
We just need to think positive!

374
00:21:59,901 --> 00:22:02,571
Finally, we're going to make some money!

375
00:22:02,654 --> 00:22:04,281
[BILLY] Wait a minute, Toni.

376
00:22:04,364 --> 00:22:09,036
Let's use the money
for system improvements first.

377
00:22:09,119 --> 00:22:10,871
[BILLY] Let's help each other
out first, okay?

378
00:22:10,954 --> 00:22:11,830
[TONI] Okay.

379
00:22:11,913 --> 00:22:14,666
I wasn't informed that
this was a foundation.

380
00:22:14,750 --> 00:22:16,293
[CHUCKLES]

381
00:22:19,838 --> 00:22:25,635
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

382
00:22:27,929 --> 00:22:30,140
<i>I'd like to ask you something</i>
<i>about your passenger.</i>

383
00:22:30,223 --> 00:22:32,350
<i>I remember what she looked like.</i>

384
00:22:32,434 --> 00:22:34,686
<i>But this is a different story.</i>
<i>Didn't you get stabbed?</i>

385
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:36,021
<i>That's our best shot right now.</i>

386
00:22:36,104 --> 00:22:38,940
<i>He's our only lead to the woman</i>
<i>who gave him the money.</i>

387
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:41,818
<i>I went to your office just before,</i>
<i>and someone was there.</i>

388
00:22:41,902 --> 00:22:44,780
<i>Didn't you say you would give me</i>
<i>a tour of your office?</i>

389
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:47,157
<i>Oliver really is my inspiration.</i>

390
00:22:47,240 --> 00:22:49,159
- [BULLIES]<i> Twig! Twig!</i>
<i>- That's enough!</i>

391
00:22:49,242 --> 00:22:50,160
[BULLIES JEER]

392
00:22:50,243 --> 00:22:52,704
<i>What kind of person</i>
<i>doesn't love their sibling?</i>

393
00:22:52,788 --> 00:22:54,039
<i>By the way, Billy,</i>

394
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:56,333
<i>I don't like that face of yours!</i>
